{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1359415-the-maya-demesnes-and-thought-forms","id":1359415,"title":"The Maya, Demesnes, and Thought-forms","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-01-06T22:15:04-08:00","id":1359415,"title":"The Maya, Demesnes, and Thought-forms","content":"Hello everyone!<br /> <br /> I've been a fan of Mage for a good while now, but I'm relatively new to the crunch. I've been working on the idea of a Focus (in M20 terms) off and on, and while there's a fair bit I still need to figure out, the main question I want to pose to the forums has to do with the subjects listed in the title. The concept is a Chaos Magician who would make use of Thought-forms as an Instrument. I had thought that it would be a neat idea to tie that in to the Demesne Background; the idea being that some of his spells might involve interactions or dealings with the entities dwelling within his personal dreamworld. Neat idea, but opens all sorts of fun metaphysical cans of worms as things in Mage are wont to do <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> And so I wanted to discuss the idea with the forums a bit, see how they might handle that? Would all thought-forms exist in the Maya, or would that be more of a High Umbra thing? Or both? Would the contents of his Demesne simply count as a Personal or Significant Instrument for the spells he can cast with them, versus other thought-forms just being regular Instruments? Is it just one of those things where it depends on your Paradigm/Storyteller? In any case, I'd love to hear feedback on the concept!<br /> <br /> As noted, I haven't worked out everything about my ideas for this Focus, but I figure I'll share what I have so far, in case it's relevant to answering the above, and because any feedback people might offer on it would be appreciated too. As noted, I'm imagining him as a Chaos Magician, with &quot;Everything is Chaos&quot; as his primary Paradigm. The central basis of his magical theory is that the base level of everything is just &quot;energy&quot;/possibility/potential (Quintessence basically), which then expresses itself physically (as matter and energy) or mentally (as thoughts, feelings, etc.); one of the central questions I have yet to answer is whether the Spirit Sphere and related phenomena are going to be regarded as a sub-category of &quot;mental/psychic&quot; in this framework, or if it should be understood as a separate &quot;in-between&quot; state, like water compared to solids and gases. From his conception, Magic is learning how to channel mental energies to act upon that base energy in all things. Because he views his magic primarily as mental energy acting upon other energies, Effects related to the Mind Sphere and those that provide information come easiest to him. Effects related to Prime and energy work would also be pretty natural to him, along with Entropy effects related to probability or luck in the form of &quot;synchromysticism.&quot; The weakest area of his Focus would be direct alterations of physical reality, which would require considerable amounts of preparation and high ritual to accomplish because (within his Paradigm) mental energy doesn't act directly upon physical reality, but instead has to act on the base energy which in turn acts on physical reality; it takes extra time to go through the extra step. My thought was that I'd represent his Focus by having him start with the Spheres of Mind, Prime, and Correspondence; Mind and Prime should be obvious, but I also see the principles of Correspondence, the connections between all things, as being an important part of his framework, given how the connection between mental and physical via a unifying energy plays such a crucial role in how his magic is supposed to achieve anything other than Mind Effects.<br /> <br /> Thanks for reading, hope you found it interesting, and that you have some thoughts of your own to share ^_^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-07T04:12:13-08:00","id":1359442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Is it just one of those things where it depends on your Paradigm/Storyteller?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, most likely.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Would all thought-forms exist in the Maya, or would that be more of a High Umbra thing? Or both? </div> </div> </div>Depends on what do you call thought-forms.<br /> <br /> Maya it's the world of <i>dreams</i>, specificly. Everything thougth can exist there, but it would be in the form of dreams and visions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Would the contents of his Demesne simply count as a Personal or Significant Instrument for the spells he can cast with them, versus other thought-forms just being regular Instruments? </div> </div> </div>They may count as personalized Instruments.<br /> <br /> That would imply your Demesne resonates with your affinity Sphere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-07T09:14:50-08:00","id":1359505,"title":"","content":"Thanks Aleph!<br /> <br /> I'll have to do some more reading from the actual theorists to make a personal decision for myself; if it's a Storyteller call, I should be able to understand it well enough to explain why it should work if I want them to work with me. I had done a little reading on the subject before, but I haven't had much time to think about it this last little while.<br /> <br /> And yes, I did forget to mention that Mind would be his Affinity Sphere. It's another thing I'm still working out the details on, but I was imagining that this character would be a Hollow One, and his Demesne might be this Transylvanian-style horror story with various characters and the conflicts between them reflecting his own inner struggles. I had been thinking a Primordial Essence, but I'm maybe leaning towards Questing now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}